    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"auto\"><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\">On Wednesday, February 3, 2016 at 4:34:57 PM UTC-5, David Knowles wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">I see that this was marked as closed:<div><a href=\"https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/issues/1239\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/issues/1239&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792462607778000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0JRr2tek8WnJ2HnNavnZI0\">https://github.com/stan-dev/stan/issues/1239</a></div><div>but with verbose=F in rstan::optimizing I&#39;m still getting output (I&#39;m on 2.9.0). Is there some other argument I need to specify as well? </div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>@Daniel, was there something more we were supposed to do on the R side for that issue? Setting verbose = FALSE suppresses the iteration progress, but still prints the settings information at the top<br><br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">STAN OPTIMIZATION COMMAND </span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">LBFGS</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>init </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> random<br>save_iterations </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>init_alpha </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.001</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>tol_obj </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1e-12</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>tol_grad </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1e-08</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>tol_param </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1e-08</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>tol_rel_obj </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">10000</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>tol_rel_grad </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1e+07</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>history_size </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>seed </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1106089312</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>initial log joint probability </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.65295</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#606\">Optimization</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> terminated normally</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>  </span><span style=\"color:#606\">Convergence</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> detected</span><span style=\"color:#660\">:</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> gradient norm </span><span style=\"color:#008\">is</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> below tolerance</span></div></code></div><br>Ben<br></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></div></blockquote></div>"
